<%# The same three states the rail's button cycles through, laid out as a choice: on the Settings page
    and in the phone's More sheet (layouts/_tabbar). Each is a SEPARATE theme controller instance
    from the rail's own; choose shares cycle's write path (html[data-theme], the cookie, the two
    metas: design-system.md rule 7) and every instance re-renders on any change (theme_controller.js
    broadcasts it), so the rail's "Switch to …" label follows a choice made here at once.
    aria-pressed is rendered by the server from the cookie on first paint and moved by the
    controller after a click.

    ONE CONTROL, NO READOUT BESIDE IT (UX audit A6): the row used to repeat a lowercase "Theme: light"
    after its own buttons, which the pressed button already says. System is the one word that needs
    explaining, and its title does it. %>
<div class="theme-choice" data-controller="theme" role="group" aria-label="Theme">
  <% hints = { "light" => "Always light", "dark" => "Always dark",
               "system" => "Follow this device's light or dark setting" } %>
  <% ShellHelper::THEMES.each do |t| %>
    <button type="button" class="btn small theme-option" data-action="theme#choose"
            data-theme-theme-param="<%= t %>" data-theme-target="option" title="<%= hints.fetch(t) %>"
            aria-pressed="<%= ui_theme == t %>"><%= t.capitalize %></button>
  <% end %>
</div>
